# .trovexignore — paths that stay REAL files on disk (trovex never proxies them).
#
# The only reason to keep a .md on disk is a file-native consumer: a docs build,
# repo tooling that reads markdown, or a human who insists on their editor.
# Everything else lives only in trovex (frontend for humans, trovex_read for agents).
#
# One glob per line; matched against both repo-relative and absolute paths.

# Repo conventions that must remain on-disk files
README.md
CHANGELOG.md
LICENSE.md
REFONTE.md

# Agent harness files the tooling reads directly
**/CLAUDE.md
**/AGENTS.md

# NOTE: niwa qa-gate artifacts (.niwa-decision.md, .niwa-*.md, anything under a
# .niwa/ workdir) are auto-exempt by the guard itself — you do NOT need to list
# them here. Pre-check any path with: trovex-md-guard.sh --check <path>

# Anything a build/site generator consumes
docs/site/**
